0.1.7

- Adjustments to the status bar to ensure text is correctly centered in vertical mode on Windows 95/98.

- Implementation of submenus under the "File" menu; although no functional code is included, the purpose is to test the status bar text.

- Fix for loading translations in submenus: previously, if a translation file existed but a specific translation string could not be found, the default text would fail to load.

0.1.6

- Status bar fixes: sizes adjusted to correctly match Windows 11, Windows 7, ReactOS, Windows 9x, and 3.11.

- Fixes to correctly handle ReactOS and Windows 7 themes.

0.1.5

- Rewrote the status bar to implement a "grip" (diagonal bars on the right side, similar to the style used in Windows 95 and later applications).

- Renamed menu, bitmap, and other variables to adopt the naming conventions commonly used in Visual C++ (H_, IDD_, IDC_, etc.).

- Added a simple implementation for a "Show/Hide Status Bar" menu option.

- Implemented icons in 16, 32, 128, and 256 sizes at 32-bit (True Color) depth, and 16 and 32 sizes at 4-bit depth (for Win16).

- Status bar fixes: the bar now displays with either a small or large height depending on the Windows version. Versions prior to Windows 2000 will always display the small bar; for Windows 2000 and later, the appropriate status bar height is displayed based on whether screen zooming is enabled.

0.1.4

- Corrections to the "About" module, as the application logo image did not fit the container space in the 32-bit version.

0.1.3

- The icons were redesigned for 16-bit and 32-bit versions; the application icon for the 16-bit version drew inspiration from the color scheme used in Notepad and WinFile, whereas the 32-bit version—having a wider color palette—looks different. Additionally, a container format was chosen to store multiple resolutions within a single .ico file; the possibility of porting this feature to the 16-bit application will be considered.

- A simple status bar was implemented, using the WinVi project as a reference. However, this was not a direct code adaptation but rather an incorporation of general concepts; furthermore, the use of pointers was avoided, as their use had previously caused Windows 3.1 to crash upon exiting after repeated program executions.

- The project's .ico files were redesigned again; the 32-bit .ico is now a container holding both 32x32 and 16x16 icons. The code was improved to provide automatic support, allowing Scryvano to automatically select the appropriate icon for display.

- Code was added to the manifest file for the 32-bit version because the text in the status bar and menus appeared blurry.

0.1.2

- Work began on the operating system language detection system; the 32-bit version works perfectly—even allowing the retrieval of regional settings—but since this functionality does not exist in Win16, the module will have to be rewritten.

- Program information was moved from "about.rc" to "main.rc" to organize the code.

- The ".rc" files were reorganized again, and the module containing the 16-bit signature was adjusted because it would not compile in OpenWatcom; language detection logic was separated for 16-bit and 32-bit versions, as they operate differently.

- The "readINIkey" function was implemented to read settings from language INI files, allowing the program's menu bar to display in either English or Spanish.

- The "About" dialog now detects the current language and applies the translation for the title and the close button.

- An "Exit" menu was implemented that successfully closes the application, along with a "New" menu (currently non-functional) and menu separators.

- An icon was assigned to the executable, and the main window now displays it in the top-left corner; in the 16-bit version, it only appears when the window is minimized.

0.1.1

- A module adapted for 16-bit and 32-bit systems (which operate quite differently) was created to retrieve the current system language. Native Windows functions are used for 32-bit systems; however, since these are unavailable for 16-bit systems, the configuration from the win.ini file is used instead.

- Program information was moved from the about.rc file to main.rc to better organize the code.

- The .rc files were reorganized again, and the module containing the 16-bit signature was adjusted because it failed to compile in OpenWatcom.

- The readINIkey function was implemented to read settings from language .ini files, allowing the program's menu bar to display in either English or Spanish (for the time being, the Spanish-English language files are not being uploaded because several improvements are being made to the system).

0.1.0

- A minimally functional implementation that only displays the main window, includes a few menus and a status bar, and can show the "About" dialog.